tags: new-client-credit, credit_mu_per_new_client

A promise of the node: the MU that it gives to a new client, one time, when
GenerateClient gives the client. The balance statement shows it as a credit movement.

The value is an amount of MU, as a decimal integer of 0 or more. Example: 4950000.

With no promise, the caller assumes no credit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
name=new-client-credit
rule=the node credits the value to each new client one time, when it gives the client
value=MU, a decimal integer of 0 or more
